## 4 AGENT ARCHETYPES

The Agent Builder recognizes 4 archetypes to scaffold new agents:

| Archetype | Characteristics | Rule Files | When to Use |
|-----------|----------------|------------|-------------|
| **Document Generator** | Template-first, section-by-section output | 5 (with Template_Config) | Producing structured documents (designs, reviews, reports) |
| **Code Generator** | Example-first, pattern-based, build-verify | 4 | Generating code, configs, specifications |
| **Analyzer** | Input analysis, scoring, report generation | 4 | Analyzing code, logs, data, producing assessments |
| **Conversational** | Discovery-driven, question-based, progressive | 4 or 5 | Estimation, planning, consulting, gathering requirements |

### Archetype Layering (Hybrid Agents)

Real-world agents may combine two archetypes — one **primary** (drives file structure) and one **secondary** (contributes patterns to specific phases). Store the secondary in state as `archetypeSecondary`.

**Examples:** WSR Email Composer (Document Generator + Conversational), Code Review (Analyzer + Document Generator), Agent Tuner (Conversational + Code Generator).

> **Archetype patterns & layering guidance**: See `@01_Guidance.mdc` Section 1

