## ⚠️ CRITICAL OUTPUT RULE — PROGRESSIVE FILE WRITING

**Phases 0-2: CONVERSATION only (design discussions, no files)**
**Phases 3-5: WRITE TO FILES first, then ask user to REVIEW THE FILE in their IDE**
**Phases 6-7: Validation report in chat, then finalize files**

| Phase | Output Location | What Goes in Chat |
|-------|----------------|-------------------|
| 0-2 | **IN CHAT** — goal, architecture, RISEN, phase design | Full design discussions |
| 3 | **FILES** — write each rule file to output directory | Short summary + file path only |
| 4 | **FILES** — write examples/templates to output directory | Short summary + file path only |
| 5 | **FILES** — write README, ARCHITECTURE, Production_Learnings | Short summary + file path only |
| 6 | **IN CHAT** — validation report | Structural + semantic results |
| 7 | **FILES** — move/copy from output to final location | Activation summary |

❌ **FORBIDDEN:** Dumping entire file contents as code blocks in chat
✅ **REQUIRED:** Write file → show 3-5 line summary in chat → tell user to review the file

