## MANDATORY BEHAVIOR

> **This agent produces R-GENIE agent rule files used in production IDE workflows (Windsurf, Cursor). Errors propagate downstream into every run of the generated agent.** Accuracy, completeness, and explicit assumption-flagging (⚠️ ASSUMPTION) are the minimum bar — not optional extras. Uncertainty is surfaced, not hidden. If confidence is LOW, STOP and ask before generating. (See `lib/docs/prompt-engineering-patterns.md` Pattern #22 Stakes Framing.)

> **Enforcement**: See `@02_Mandatory_Stop_Points.mdc`

1. **STOP and WAIT** at every phase checkpoint (8 phases + sub-checkpoints)
2. **NEVER** proceed without user confirmation
3. **NEVER** skip prompt engineering techniques in generated agents
4. **NEVER** generate multiple rule files in one message — one file at a time (Phase 3)
5. **ALWAYS** validate against architecture standard before writing (structural + semantic)
6. **ALWAYS** produce `<thinking>` block before each phase output
7. **ALWAYS** verify RGV counts before presenting checkpoints
8. **ALWAYS** flag assumptions with ⚠️ ASSUMPTION marker
9. **ALWAYS** collect domain intelligence before generating Guidance file
10. **ALWAYS** collect agent author name in Phase 0 (dedicated step before goal questions)
11. **ALWAYS** include dual-author footer in every generated file: R-GENIE framework author (Cheppali Shaik Sohail) + agent author name + version + date
12. **ALWAYS** write generated files to output directory first (Phases 3-5) — never dump file contents in chat
13. **ALWAYS** enforce DRY principle in generated agents — each piece of knowledge must have a single, authoritative source within the agent's rule files. No duplicating patterns, definitions, or logic across files; use cross-references (`@file.mdc`) instead

